Z||000000||stimpy||06-13-2001||12:00 AM||||I'm checking out enrolling with Netflix. It seems lke a good deal, but how does it work in reality? Does anyone have it? Are you happy with it? What kind of turnaround is there on getting the new discs back when you return them?<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||06-13-2001||12:26 AM||||I'm pretty sure I got wrapped up in that a while ago.  Even after I sent back their DVDs, they kept charging me and charging me.  We finally had to cancel the credit card and get another (with a different account number) to get them off our backs.  Maybe they've changed by now, but I wouldn't count on it.  Just my opinion.  Maybe others have had better experiences with them.<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||06-13-2001||12:36 AM||||My folks started using them a few months ago. I'm thinking of joining too. You create a list of movies. They send you 4 of them right away. Then after you watch one (or all), You put it in a supplied envelope and drop it in the mail. Once they receive it they send the next one (or 4) on your list.<BR>It takes about a week for the transfer. So if you sent it in on Monday morning, you get the new one by Saturday afternoon usually but occasionally Monday. (Depends on the mail)||||reg||1
